=== PARITY (vs web VinDecoder.tsx, 46 lines) ===
  Data sources -> the web source's ONLY hook is `useTranslation`; the decode is a pure,
    synchronous, local lookup chain in a `useMemo` with NO data hook, NO network, NO cache. The
    native parity binds through a local P1/S8 state holder (VinDecoderModel) that owns `input` and
    DERIVES `result` on read (the @Observable analogue of the web `useMemo`). The view performs no
    HTTP — there is none to perform.
  Decode -> VinDecoderAdapter.decode is a faithful port: `vin.length < 11` -> nil (no result);
    otherwise `vin.toUpperCase()` then positional reads — WMI = chars 1-3, model = char 4,
    drive = char 8, year = char 10, plant = char 11, serial = `slice(11)`. Reference tables
    (VIN_MANUFACTURERS / VIN_MODELS / VIN_DRIVE / VIN_YEAR / VIN_PLANT) are ported verbatim from the
    web devtools constants.ts (vehicle reference data, not localized copy — exactly as the web
    hardcodes them). A position with no table entry -> nil -> the view renders the localized
    "Unknown" the web composes via `?? t('Unknown')`. Entry order (mfr, model, drive, year, plant,
    serial) mirrors the web `Object.entries(decoded)` iteration. PROVEN by executed tests below
    against the web example VIN 5YJ3E1EA1NF000001 -> Tesla (USA) / Model 3 / Dual Motor AWD / 2022 /
    Fremont, CA / 000001.
  Composition -> web ToolCard (cyan, Car icon) + Input (label t('Vin'), Car icon, example value) +
    `{decoded && <grid sm:grid-cols-2>}` -> native glass ToolCard + single-line field + adaptive
    LazyVGrid of label/value tiles. Atomic shared components (ToolCard, Input) are covered by the P4
    component-library bundle; this surface composes its chrome from the design Tokens + TSGlassPanel.
  i18n -> every string resolves through the P1/S10 facade (VinDecoderStrings, table "VinDecoder").
    Source keys reproduced verbatim: "Vin Decoder", "Vin Decoder Desc", "Vin", "Unknown",
    devtools.utils.vin_{mfr,model,drive,year,plant,serial}. The web catalog leaves the
    devtools.utils.vin_* labels unfilled (it renders the raw key); the native catalog supplies
    proper copy (Manufacturer / Model / Drivetrain / Model Year / Plant / Serial). No English
    literal lives in the view body — only facade keys + their fallbacks.
  a11y -> VoiceOver label + hint on the VIN field; each result tile is a combined element with
    label + value; the icon glyphs are accessibility-hidden; Dynamic Type via the type tokens;
    Reduce Motion honored (TSAnimation.standard returns nil under reduce-motion).

